    q: "What is the color wheel, and what's the difference between complementary and analogous color schemes?",
    a: "The color wheel arranges hues in a circle based on their relationships. A complementary scheme pairs colors opposite each other on the wheel (e.g. blue and orange) — high contrast, good for making an accent (a CTA) pop against a base color. An analogous scheme uses colors next to each other on the wheel (e.g. blue, teal, green) — naturally harmonious and low-contrast, good for a cohesive, calm palette but requiring extra thought to establish sufficient hierarchy since the colors are inherently similar.",
