    cat: "UI",
    q: "What should a designer specify about keyboard navigation and focus order?",
    a: "The logical tab order through a screen (should generally follow the visual reading order, not the arbitrary DOM order a developer might default to), a clearly visible focus indicator on every interactive element (not removed for aesthetics — a common and serious accessibility regression), keyboard equivalents for any mouse-only interaction (drag-and-drop needs a keyboard alternative), and correct focus-trapping behavior for modals/dialogs (focus should move into the modal on open, cycle only within it while open, and return to the triggering element on close — not leak back out to the page behind it).",
