    q: "Distinguish which research method fits each question: 'how satisfied are 10,000 users with support?' vs. 'why do users abandon step 2 of onboarding?' vs. 'can users complete a refund request unaided?'",
    sol: "'How satisfied are 10,000 users...' -> survey (quantitative, needs scale/reach). 'Why do users abandon step 2...' -> interviews or session-recording analysis paired with follow-up interviews (qualitative, needs to understand reasoning). 'Can users complete a refund request unaided...' -> usability testing (observing real task completion directly).",
    exp: "Each question's shape ('how many/satisfied,' 'why,' 'can they do X') maps directly to the method built to answer that specific type of question.",
