    q: "Given a WCAG AA requirement, is white text (#FFFFFF) on a medium blue background (#4A90D9) sufficient for normal-size body text, and what would you do if not?",
    sol: "That specific pairing's contrast ratio is roughly 2.5:1 — well below the 4.5:1 required for normal text at AA. Fix by darkening the blue background (a deeper blue reaches the needed ratio while staying visually 'blue'), increasing the text size/weight to qualify for the lower 3:1 large-text threshold if that fits the context, or choosing a different background color entirely and reserving the current blue for a large graphical element rather than a text background.",
    exp: "A visually pleasant color pairing can still fail a hard numeric accessibility requirement — always verify with an actual contrast checker rather than eyeballing it.",
