    sol: "Passing contrast checks individually doesn't guarantee relative hierarchy — if every element has similar contrast levels against the background, nothing stands out even though each one is individually 'compliant.' Fix by increasing the relative contrast gap specifically for the primary action beyond what secondary elements have (a stronger, more saturated fill color for the primary button vs. a lighter or outlined style for secondary ones), while keeping every individual pairing still within WCAG minimums.",
